PS:
Design and deploy a static website on a cloud virtual machine/Instance. Configure the server
and networking settings so that the website is publicly accessible and can be updated remotely.

1. Create Instance
    a. Network settings - Allow SSH traffic from Anywhere, This allows you to connect securely from your laptop.
                        - Allow HTTP traffic from Internet, This opens port 80 so website becomes public.
2. Go where the .pem key is present and give permissions using - chmod 400 <key-name>.pem
3. Connect to instance - ssh -i <key-name>.pem ubuntu@<public-ip>
4. Set up apache
    - Install - sudo apt install apache2 -y
    - Start - sudo systemctl start apache2
    - Enable - sudo systemctl enable apache2
    - Status - sudo systemctl status apache2
5. Verify apache, open - http://INSTANCE_PUBLIC_IP - should see apache page
6. cd /var/www/html - when ls gives index.html, remove that using - sudo rm /var/www/html/index.html
7. sudo nano <file.name>, put the content
8. go to the same ip
9. if any error - sudo chmod -R 755 /var/www/html, sudo systemctl restart apache2